WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.543 --> 00:00:08.913
♪ ♪

00:00:07.745 --> 00:00:10.814
&gt;&gt; John: IT'S BEEN FIVE YEARS

00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:12.316
SINCE THE WHITE SMOKE AT THE

00:00:10.948 --> 00:00:13.817
SISTINE CHAPEL INDICATED A NEW

00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:18.956
POPE HAD BEEN NAMED.

00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:23.027
TONIGHT BRET BAIER TALKS WITH

00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:26.030
CARDINAL DONALD WUERL.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.830
&gt;&gt; THANKS, JOHN.

00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:28.265
TOMORROW IS THE FIFTH

00:00:26.964 --> 00:00:28.632
ANNIVERSARY OF POPE FRANCIS'

00:00:28.399 --> 00:00:30.668
ELECTION.

00:00:28.766 --> 00:00:32.870
TO TALK ABOUT THAT, JOINING ME

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.737
NOW CARDINAL DONALD WUERL,

00:00:33.003 --> 00:00:35.706
ARCHBISHOP OF WASHINGTON, AND TO

00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:36.473
WEIGH IN ON THE LAST FIVE YEARS

00:00:35.839 --> 00:00:37.374
OF THE PAPACY.

00:00:36.607 --> 00:00:38.676
THANK YOU FOR BEING HERE.

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:39.910
&gt;&gt; YOU ARE WELCOME.

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:43.013
IT'S A GREAT JOY TO BE BACK TO

00:00:40.044 --> 00:00:44.048
BE WITH YOU.

00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:46.250
AND TO THINK, CELEBRATING THE

00:00:44.181 --> 00:00:48.218
FIFTH ANNIVERSARY OF

00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:51.021
POPE FRANCIS.

00:00:48.352 --> 00:00:56.060
I THINK THE IMPACT OF

00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:57.828
POPE FRANCIS IS PEOPLE SEE IN

00:00:56.193 --> 00:01:00.030
HIM, HE BEARS WITNESS WITH HIS

00:00:57.962 --> 00:01:02.232
LIFE, NOT JUST HIS WORDS.

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:07.204
HIS WHOLE IMPACT, AS I SEE IT,

00:01:02.366 --> 00:01:08.706
IS HE'S OPENED UP THE CHURCH IN

00:01:07.338 --> 00:01:09.607
NO WAY THAT PEOPLE FEEL THEY ARE

00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:12.643
MUCH MORE WELCOME.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:14.411
HE SAYS TO THEM, THERE IS SPACE

00:01:12.776 --> 00:01:14.745
FOR ALL OF US HERE IN THIS

00:01:14.545 --> 00:01:16.647
CHURCH.

00:01:14.878 --> 00:01:16.981
&gt;&gt; I HAVE SEEN THE MAP OF HIS

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.817
TRAVEL.

00:01:17.114 --> 00:01:20.417
IT'S QUITE SOMETHING.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.819
IT'S EXTENSIVE.

00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:23.187
&gt;&gt; IT IS.

00:01:21.952 --> 00:01:25.422
WHEN HE WAS ELECTED, HE SAID I

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.257
DON'T THINK I WILL BE MOVING

00:01:25.556 --> 00:01:27.558
AROUND AS MUCH AS PREVIOUS

00:01:27.391 --> 00:01:28.292
POPES.

00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:30.327
THAT TURNED OUT NOT TO BE TRUE

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:33.864
AT ALL.

00:01:30.461 --> 00:01:35.633
FOR AS OLD AS HE IS, HE

00:01:33.998 --> 00:01:37.167
CONTINUES TO CARRY OUT THE

00:01:35.766 --> 00:01:37.968
SCHEDULE OF SOMEONE 20 YEARS

00:01:37.768 --> 00:01:39.670
YOUNGER.

00:01:38.102 --> 00:01:40.004
HE'S HAVING AN IMPACT EVERYWHERE

00:01:39.803 --> 00:01:42.840
HE GOES.

00:01:40.137 --> 00:01:43.440
&gt;&gt; Bret: HE MET WITH

00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:44.308
PRESIDENT TRUMP AND

00:01:43.574 --> 00:01:45.843
PRESIDENT TRUMP REMARKED ON THE

00:01:44.441 --> 00:01:47.011
CONVERSATION THEY HAD.

00:01:45.976 --> 00:01:49.279
THEY ARE CONSERVATIVES I GUESS

00:01:47.144 --> 00:01:51.615
YOU WOULD SAY IN THE U.S. WHO

00:01:49.413 --> 00:01:54.151
ARE SKEPTICAL OF SOME OF THE

00:01:51.749 --> 00:01:55.085
POLITICS PERHAPS, HOW HE

00:01:54.284 --> 00:01:55.452
EXPRESSES THE IDEOLOGY

00:01:55.219 --> 00:01:57.955
SOMETIMES.

00:01:55.586 --> 00:02:01.825
HOW DO YOU DEAL WITH THAT FOR

00:01:58.088 --> 00:02:03.227
YOUR CONGREGATIONS HERE?

00:02:01.959 --> 00:02:04.495
TALKING ABOUT IDEOLOGY AND

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.795
POLITICS WHEN IT COMES TO THE

00:02:04.628 --> 00:02:07.131
PULP.

00:02:04.928 --> 00:02:08.565
&gt;&gt; ONE OF THE WONDERFUL THINGS

00:02:07.264 --> 00:02:12.436
ABOUT POPE FRANCIS IS HE DOESN'T

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:14.038
SEEM TO BE INHIBITED BY

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:16.774
CATEGORIES, BY LABELING.

00:02:14.171 --> 00:02:20.678
HE SAYS WHAT HE THINKS ON A

00:02:16.907 --> 00:02:22.513
PARTICULAR TOPIC, AND HE SAYS IT

00:02:20.811 --> 00:02:23.247
NOT IN POLITICAL TERMS AND NOT

00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:25.649
IN IDEOLOGICAL TERMS.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.517
YOU ARE RIGHT, THOSE ARE --

00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:28.352
THERE ARE THOSE WHO WOULD TRY TO

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.752
PUT IT IN ONE OF THOSE

00:02:28.485 --> 00:02:32.289
CATEGORIES.

00:02:28.886 --> 00:02:33.490
I THINK THAT'S ONE OF THE

00:02:32.423 --> 00:02:34.058
ATTRACTIVE THINGS ABOUT

00:02:33.624 --> 00:02:35.259
POPE FRANCIS.

00:02:34.191 --> 00:02:36.193
PEOPLE REALIZE HE'S JUST

00:02:35.392 --> 00:02:40.631
SPEAKING FROM HIS HEART.

00:02:36.326 --> 00:02:40.931
IT'S NOT FROM SOME PRECONCEIVED

